course: dictionary
lesson: 13759
title: Words that travel between worlds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Long words often hide smaller words you already know. Interplanetary has three parts: inter means between, planet is a planet, and -ary turns it into a describing word. Put them together and you get between planets, or travelling from one planet to another.
explain: «Scientists sent an interplanetary probe to study Mars.» The clues are probe and Mars. A probe is a machine that travels far away, so this must be a trip between planets. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Interplanetary fits, because the sentence is about space.
explain: The word also tells the reader the topic. «The science club read a book about interplanetary missions.» Missions and planets show that this is about space beyond Earth, not about a school trip or a day at the beach.
fact: Interplanetary means between planets, or travelling from one planet to another.
fact: Inter means between, and you can see it in other words such as international, which means between nations.
fact: Interplanetary is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in interplanetary space or interplanetary travel.
fact: «Interplanetary» tells the reader the topic is space beyond Earth.
fact: When you meet a long word, look for parts you know, such as inter or planet, and check the meaning in the sentence.
exercise: «The crew trained for years before the interplanetary journey.» What does interplanetary mean here? | *Travelling from one planet to another | Under the sea | Happening in the same town | Very cold and icy
exercise: What does the part inter mean in interplanetary? | *Between | Around the edge | Under | Far away from home
exercise: Mia says interplanetary is a word about the sea. Why is she wrong? | She is right, it is about the sea | Interplanetary means under water | *The word is about space, between planets, not the sea | It means the sea is between planets
test: «The interplanetary mission will carry a robot to Jupiter.» What does interplanetary tell you about the mission? | It is a mission in a local park | It is a mission under the sea | *It travels between planets, in space beyond Earth | It is about cooking food
test: Which sentence uses interplanetary correctly? | The school lunch menu was interplanetary | My cat's bed is interplanetary and soft | The sea is interplanetary, full of fish | *Astronauts dreamed of interplanetary travel to Venus
exam: Is interplanetary a good word for «The rocket flew from Earth to Mars»? | No, because it means grey and wet | *Yes, because the rocket travels between planets | No, because it means very old | No, because it means very hungry
